# Broad configuration sweep: every software/configuration axis varies.
#
# Use `throughput-matrix.plan` when only connection count, bitrate, runtime,
# ingress, and encryption should move. This file is deliberately much larger:
# it exposes interactions among topology, pacing, encryption, workers,
# promotion, socket buffers, bonding, and CPU pinning.
#
# Earlier ladders held one of the two fixed:
#   scaling-ladder  constant ~300 Mbps aggregate, N varied  -> isolates per-connection cost
#   bw-ladder       constant 2 Mbps/conn, N varied          -> aggregate rises with N
# Neither can separate "many connections" from "many bytes", because in
# both the two move together. Varying them independently does, at the
# cost of 4x the cells.
#
# Raw product: 6 runtimes x 5 ingress x 2 egress x 4 encryption x 4 connections x 4 bitrate
# x 3 workers x 4 promotion x 2 cookie-routing x 2 batch x 2 sock-buf
# x 2 connect-concurrency x 3 bond x 2 pin = 4,423,680 cells.
#
# The harness enumerates the raw product and applies capability filtering
# without retaining all raw cells. It retains one
# representative for inert axes, keeps promotion/cookie controls only where
# reuseport admission can observe them, keeps batching only where mio has a
# shared-socket batched path, keeps pinning only where glommio applies it,
# keeps one sender-worker and connect-concurrency representative for shared
# egress (one socket has one owning runtime loop), and removes bond groups
# larger than half the connection population. Identical-four-tuple bonded
# cells remain valid protocol/group exercises because SRT Socket IDs demux the
# legs, but they do not provide independent network paths and therefore must
# not be interpreted as a path-diversity/failover benchmark. Within
# reuseport-multi with no bond group, relocate and bonded collapse to never,
# so only never/all are retained. With the values below that leaves 67,200
# executable, non-duplicate cells.
# This is intentionally exhaustive across meaningful behavior, not a default
# smoke test.
#
# Run with:
#   srt-bench matrix --plan docs/plans/full-matrix.plan \
#     --secs 10 --reps 1 --order interleaved --seed 0 \
#     --out scratch/full-all.tsv
#
# `interleaved` is the recommended first pass: it rotates the broad axes and
# repetitions so the early output samples the whole space. `random` is also
# available with a recorded `--seed`; the default preserves Cartesian order.
#
# Resumable: re-running skips cells already present in the output file,
# so an interrupted sweep continues rather than restarting.

runtime             = mio,tokio,smol,monoio,glommio,compio
ingress             = per-port,shared-pool:1,shared-pool:4,reuseport-multi:4,reuseport-single:4
egress              = per-connection,shared-socket
encryption          = plain,128,192,256
connections         = 50,200,600,1200
bitrate             = 250000,1000000,4000000,8000000
workers             = 1,2,3
promotion           = never,relocate,bonded,all
cookie-routing      = on,off
batch               = on,off
sock-buf            = default,16m
connect-concurrency = 1,50
bond                = none,broadcast:64,backup:64
pin                 = off,on
